WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.830 --> 00:00:05.420
Jamie Foxx has been entertaining millions
for decades, but away from the spotlight,

00:00:05.420 --> 00:00:07.900
his family members have kept drifting away.

00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:12.350
This is the tragic true story of the man born
Eric Marlon Bishop.

00:00:12.350 --> 00:00:16.641
Jamie Foxx's life was riddled with roadblocks
pretty much right from the start, as he was

00:00:16.641 --> 00:00:19.900
abandoned by both of his parents when he was
just a baby.

00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:24.140
But it wasn't a completely tragic origin story,
as he did have other people in his life to

00:00:24.140 --> 00:00:25.140
look after him.

00:00:25.140 --> 00:00:28.150
As he recalled to O, The Oprah Magazine in
2005,

00:00:28.150 --> 00:00:31.520
"My grandparents adopted me when I was 7 months
old.

00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:35.400
I was never short on the love of a mother
and father, though it came from an earlier

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:36.829
generation of family."

00:00:36.829 --> 00:00:40.760
The woman that Foxx calls his grandmother,
Estelle Marie Talley, is actually not his

00:00:40.760 --> 00:00:44.880
biological grandmother, but instead, the adoptive
mother of his mother.

00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:50.110
While his parents left him behind, he couldn't
help but miss them and hold out hope for them to return.

00:00:50.110 --> 00:00:51.110
As he recalled,

00:00:51.110 --> 00:00:52.670
"[My mom] was so fly and good-looking.

00:00:52.670 --> 00:00:55.890
We were country, but my mom was straight city.

00:00:55.890 --> 00:00:59.440
She had the new hair, the gold earrings, the
Stingray Corvette."

00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:02.470
However, Foxx had more mixed feelings about
his father.

00:01:02.470 --> 00:01:03.470
As he put it,

00:01:03.470 --> 00:01:08.759
"Why couldn't he drive 28 miles to check on
a son who passed a football more than 1,000 yards?

00:01:08.759 --> 00:01:11.690
I think some of his absence has to do with
his being a Muslim.

00:01:11.690 --> 00:01:17.020
He drew a line in the sand: 'I'm a Muslim,
and since you're not, I can't be your father.'"

00:01:17.020 --> 00:01:21.360
Jamie Foxx always had ambitions to make it
big, but his original goals were a little

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:25.869
different, as the Texas-bred entertainer hoped
to one day play professional football.

00:01:25.869 --> 00:01:29.150
Specifically, he wanted to be the quarterback
for the Dallas Cowboys.

00:01:29.150 --> 00:01:34.690
And this wasn't a mere pipe dream, as he actually
showed plenty of promise on the field back in the day.

00:01:34.690 --> 00:01:38.659
While playing on the football squad at Terrell
High School, Foxx became the first quarterback

00:01:38.659 --> 00:01:42.439
to pass for more than 1,000 yards in the school's
entire history.

00:01:42.439 --> 00:01:46.900
Ultimately, though, sports stardom just wasn't
in the cards, as he wasn't blessed with the

00:01:46.900 --> 00:01:50.340
right physical dimensions to make it all the
way to the pros.

00:01:50.340 --> 00:01:55.080
Nevertheless, Terrell High made sure that
his athletic legacy lived on and also named

00:01:55.080 --> 00:01:57.200
their performing arts center after him.

00:01:57.400 --> 00:01:58.480
"Terrell, baby."

00:01:58.480 --> 00:02:02.479
While his football dreams didn't work out,
Jamie Foxx still had a bright future ahead

00:02:02.479 --> 00:02:06.869
of him, which was clear when he attended the
United States International University in

00:02:06.869 --> 00:02:09.319
San Diego on a music scholarship.

00:02:09.319 --> 00:02:13.870
He was excited about finally leaving behind
the racial bigotry of rural Texas, and he

00:02:13.870 --> 00:02:16.170
hoped that things would be different at college.

00:02:16.170 --> 00:02:18.160
As he recalled to O, the Oprah Magazine,

00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:22.730
"I'd come from a world where blacks and whites
were separated by the town's railroad tracks

00:02:22.730 --> 00:02:27.260
[...] But at the university, there were people
from 81 different countries."

00:02:27.260 --> 00:02:31.989
Reality soon came crashing down on him, though,
as Foxx learned that despite his new diverse

00:02:31.989 --> 00:02:35.060
surroundings, his race was still going to
be a roadblock.

00:02:35.060 --> 00:02:39.570
He was partially excluded from his college
music department because of his skin color.

00:02:39.570 --> 00:02:41.050
As he revealed to People Magazine,

00:02:41.050 --> 00:02:44.930
"They wouldn't let me go on the stage but
they would let me behind the curtain because

00:02:44.930 --> 00:02:47.599
there weren't any African Americans in the
production.

00:02:47.599 --> 00:02:51.760
So I would sing in the back, and I would just
sing the parts they needed me [for]."

00:02:51.760 --> 00:02:58.460
In 2004, Jamie Foxx's grandmother Estelle
Marie Talley passed away at her home in Terrell, Texas.

00:02:58.460 --> 00:03:02.739
All of her grandson's memories of her raising
him overwhelmed him in the wake of her death.

00:03:02.739 --> 00:03:03.879
As he recalled to GQ,

00:03:03.879 --> 00:03:09.239
"I remember those hands wipin' tears from
my face [...] Those hands had me stuck at the casket.

00:03:09.239 --> 00:03:10.239
I was stuck.

00:03:10.239 --> 00:03:11.709
I couldn't move."

00:03:11.709 --> 00:03:15.360
Foxx shared a genuine, authentic bond with
his grandmother that he doesn't have with

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:16.739
too many other people.

00:03:16.739 --> 00:03:17.739
As he put it,

00:03:17.739 --> 00:03:20.970
"If you could go to heaven right now and say,
'Where is Estelle Talley?'

00:03:20.970 --> 00:03:22.480
Do that interview.

00:03:22.480 --> 00:03:23.630
Because that's who knows me.

00:03:23.630 --> 00:03:24.780
Nobody else."

00:03:24.780 --> 00:03:28.491
While Foxx was really shaken up at the time,
in the years since, he's looked back at his

00:03:28.491 --> 00:03:31.370
experiences with his grandmother with nothing
but love.

00:03:31.370 --> 00:03:36.450
In 2019, he celebrated her birthday on Instagram
with an old picture and a caption that read,

00:03:36.450 --> 00:03:37.650
"My rock...

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:38.709
Miss u always"

00:03:38.709 --> 00:03:42.909
"'Act like you got some sense' is what she
would tell me all the time."

00:03:42.909 --> 00:03:47.629
While his grandmother's death was heartbreaking,
a glimmer of hope came out of it for Foxx,

00:03:47.629 --> 00:03:50.409
as his father actually showed up at her funeral.

00:03:50.409 --> 00:03:55.209
After years of absence, he was tentatively
testing the waters to rejoin the family.

00:03:55.209 --> 00:03:57.799
As Foxx recalled to GQ, his dad asked him,

00:03:57.799 --> 00:03:58.980
"Are you my son?

00:03:58.980 --> 00:04:00.280
Are you not my son?

00:04:00.280 --> 00:04:02.269
I wanna reconcile but I'm scared."

00:04:02.269 --> 00:04:04.250
Foxx then opened his arms and told his father,

00:04:04.250 --> 00:04:05.799
"You don't have to be scared.

00:04:05.799 --> 00:04:07.160
It is what it is."

00:04:07.160 --> 00:04:10.510
Alas, after the funeral, his father disappeared
yet again.

00:04:10.510 --> 00:04:12.220
Still, he remains hopeful.

00:04:12.220 --> 00:04:17.380
A decade after the funeral, Foxx told The
Sunday Times in 2014 that the door remains

00:04:17.380 --> 00:04:21.500
open for his father, partly in hopes of settling
some of the questions that have plagued him

00:04:21.500 --> 00:04:22.900
for years, like:

00:04:22.900 --> 00:04:24.090
"What happened?

00:04:24.090 --> 00:04:25.090
Where were you?

00:04:25.090 --> 00:04:26.350
Were you stricken with something?

00:04:26.350 --> 00:04:28.470
Could you not make it?"

00:04:28.470 --> 00:04:33.460
While Foxx's biological dad was never around,
he was able to find a consistent father figure

00:04:33.460 --> 00:04:37.050
in the form of his mother's second ex-husband,
George Dixon.

00:04:37.050 --> 00:04:38.690
As Foxx recalled to GQ,

00:04:38.690 --> 00:04:40.650
"My stepfather's into sports.

00:04:40.650 --> 00:04:44.340
When I was running track, I'd always be looking
for my stepfather.

00:04:44.340 --> 00:04:46.960
Sometimes he'd stand outside the fence and
say, 'C'mon, man!'

00:04:46.960 --> 00:04:48.350
And I'd make it.

00:04:48.350 --> 00:04:49.680
I'd make the high jump."

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:54.550
But in a tragic turn of events that seems
almost too cruel to be true, Foxx almost lost

00:04:54.550 --> 00:04:56.340
his stepfather as well.

00:04:56.340 --> 00:05:00.680
Dixon was sentenced to seven years of prison
on a drug charge, which was particularly hard

00:05:00.680 --> 00:05:01.680
on Foxx.

00:05:01.680 --> 00:05:06.090
He felt like this man whom he admired so much
had failed him, though he wasn't going to

00:05:06.090 --> 00:05:07.660
just kick him to the curb.

00:05:07.660 --> 00:05:11.520
So when he got out of prison, Foxx extended
an invitation.

00:05:11.520 --> 00:05:12.520
As he recalled,

00:05:12.520 --> 00:05:14.140
"I said, 'You are gonna live with me.'

00:05:14.140 --> 00:05:15.970
I got his parole changed.

00:05:15.970 --> 00:05:19.080
I said, 'I will save your life, because your
kids are something special."

00:05:19.080 --> 00:05:21.100
"That father taught me everything.

00:05:21.100 --> 00:05:26.849
Taught me how to throw a football, um, um,
basketball, taught me how to play tennis."

00:05:26.849 --> 00:05:30.820
His stepfather isn't the only family member
that Jamie Foxx has taken in and forgiven.

00:05:30.820 --> 00:05:35.550
As he revealed during a 2020 appearance on
The Graham Norton Show, his relationship with

00:05:35.550 --> 00:05:39.950
his mother had improved to the point that
they'd been living together since 2008.

00:05:39.950 --> 00:05:44.080
Foxx was thankful to have his mom back in
his life, but he also admitted that it wasn't

00:05:44.080 --> 00:05:47.400
an immediate adjustment to wholesome mother-son
bonding.

00:05:47.400 --> 00:05:51.600
The road to reconciliation can be rocky, and
there was a lot of his childhood that he still

00:05:51.600 --> 00:05:52.900
needed to process.

00:05:52.900 --> 00:05:55.330
As he explained to The Sunday Times in 2014,

00:05:55.330 --> 00:05:57.660
"We're trying to learn about each other.

00:05:57.660 --> 00:06:01.669
You realize certain things that you missed
when you were growing up, like, 'Oh, I do

00:06:01.669 --> 00:06:03.300
that because of that.'"

00:06:03.300 --> 00:06:07.020
Jamie Foxx has been open about his struggle
with substance abuse and its effect on his

00:06:07.020 --> 00:06:08.410
overall health.

00:06:08.410 --> 00:06:13.050
This has included drug-induced mental breaks
that were bad enough that his family had to

00:06:13.050 --> 00:06:14.050
intervene.

00:06:14.050 --> 00:06:15.440
As he recalled in an interview with HipHollywood,

00:06:15.440 --> 00:06:20.330
"When that [was] happening, I was lucky enough
to have people like my sister, like my family,

00:06:20.330 --> 00:06:23.870
say, 'Yo, you can't go out right now, because
you're talking crazy."

00:06:23.870 --> 00:06:29.840
In 2005, Foxx was partying hard after being
nominated for an Academy Award for Ray.

00:06:29.840 --> 00:06:33.690
Then one week before the Oscars, he got a
call from Oprah Winfrey, who stepped in to

00:06:33.690 --> 00:06:34.760
set him straight.

00:06:34.760 --> 00:06:39.132
"She says, all of this gallivanting and all
this kind of shit, that's not what you want to do."

00:06:39.132 --> 00:06:43.410
Winfrey put together an informal intervention
that helped Foxx realize that he needed to

00:06:43.410 --> 00:06:45.690
take a step back from his reckless lifestyle.

00:06:45.690 --> 00:06:50.180
"You know, sometimes, in the Oscars, the characters
that they award, sometimes they're a little

00:06:50.180 --> 00:06:51.180
fractured-"

00:06:51.180 --> 00:06:52.180
"This is bigger than you."

00:06:52.180 --> 00:06:53.180
"Yeah, it's way bigger."

00:06:53.180 --> 00:06:58.280
On more than one occasion, Jamie Foxx has
ruffled a few feathers with tasteless comments

00:06:58.280 --> 00:07:00.030
and controversial behavior.

00:07:00.030 --> 00:07:04.900
For example, during a 2009 episode of his
radio show The Foxxhole, he said about Miley

00:07:04.900 --> 00:07:06.910
Cyrus, who was 17 at the time,

00:07:06.910 --> 00:07:10.851
"Make a sex tape and grow up [...] Get some
crack in your pipe [...] Catch chlamydia on

00:07:10.851 --> 00:07:12.440
a bicycle seat."

00:07:12.440 --> 00:07:17.400
Then in 2015, Foxx introduced Caitlyn Jenner
at the iHeartRadio Music Awards, which was

00:07:17.400 --> 00:07:21.470
around the time that rumors had started to
leak about her gender transition.

00:07:21.470 --> 00:07:23.070
Foxx commented during the ceremony,

00:07:23.070 --> 00:07:25.320
"He's doing a his and her duet all by himself.

00:07:25.320 --> 00:07:28.410
Look, I'm just busting your balls — while
I still can."

00:07:28.410 --> 00:07:32.500
Foxx has also come under fire for defending
controversial rappers like Kanye West and

00:07:32.500 --> 00:07:37.510
Chris Brown, as well as mocking deaf people,
and exhibiting cruel behavior on sets.

00:07:37.510 --> 00:07:42.220
He's also even been accused of sexual assault,
a claim that he has denied.

00:07:42.220 --> 00:07:45.750
Jamie Foxx was always close with his sister
Deondra Dixon.

00:07:45.750 --> 00:07:48.800
She had Down syndrome, and he often served
as her caretaker.

00:07:48.800 --> 00:07:52.960
When people asked him if she was too much
of a burden, he would emphatically say no.

00:07:52.960 --> 00:07:55.190
As he told GQ in 2004,

00:07:55.190 --> 00:07:59.300
"If I can't take care of my sister who has
Down syndrome, what will people think of me

00:07:59.300 --> 00:08:03.790
sittin' up in Mr. Chow, drinking Dom Pérignon
and doing interviews with GQ?

00:08:03.790 --> 00:08:06.090
[...] So, no, we won't have any of that."

00:08:06.090 --> 00:08:10.560
In 2020, Foxx took to Instagram to share the
tragic news of Dixon's passing.

00:08:10.560 --> 00:08:15.621
He posted several photos of the two of them
together along with a caption that read in part:

00:08:15.621 --> 00:08:21.389
"My heart is shattered into a million pieces...
my beautiful loving sister Deondra has transitioned...

00:08:21.389 --> 00:08:24.550
I say transitioned because she will always
be alive...

00:08:24.550 --> 00:08:27.569
anyone who knew my sis... knew that she was
a bright light."

00:08:27.569 --> 00:08:29.539
"What have you learned from Deondra?"

00:08:29.539 --> 00:08:31.530
"Learned how to live."

00:08:31.530 --> 00:08:37.039
For many years, Jamie Foxx's daughter Corinne
Foxx experienced debilitating pain and nausea

00:08:37.039 --> 00:08:38.839
during her menstrual cycle.

00:08:38.839 --> 00:08:42.789
She thought this was normal, as several doctors
brushed off her concerns.

00:08:42.789 --> 00:08:44.159
As she explained to Today,

00:08:44.159 --> 00:08:47.430
"There's a lot of medical gaslighting that
goes into this journey.

00:08:47.430 --> 00:08:51.990
I think women of color, especially, are often
silenced or not believed when they come in

00:08:51.990 --> 00:08:53.209
with symptoms."

00:08:53.209 --> 00:08:58.380
Corinne was eventually diagnosed with stage
4 endometriosis, a condition in which abnormal

00:08:58.380 --> 00:09:02.700
tissue grows outside the uterus, causing extreme
discomfort.

00:09:02.700 --> 00:09:07.470
She even had to undergo surgery in 2018 because
the pain was so debilitating.

00:09:07.470 --> 00:09:12.870
She then became an ambassador for the Endometriosis
Foundation of America, as well as an executive

00:09:12.870 --> 00:09:18.060
producer of Below the Belt, a documentary
raising awareness about the condition.

00:09:18.060 --> 00:09:21.990
After the release of the film, her dad took
to Instagram to applaud his daughter for powering

00:09:21.990 --> 00:09:25.980
through such a severe struggle and making
something positive out of it.

00:09:25.980 --> 00:09:26.980
As he wrote,

00:09:26.980 --> 00:09:31.000
"So proud of my daughter [...] Please check
out [...] Below The Belt... you will be blown

00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:34.380
away by the courage the women possess in this
film."

00:09:34.380 --> 00:09:38.600
Things took a very scary turn for Jamie Foxx
on April 12, 2023.

00:09:38.600 --> 00:09:43.269
Corinne Foxx posted on social media that her
father had suffered a "medical complication,"

00:09:43.269 --> 00:09:46.060
though she didn't provide any further explanation.

00:09:46.060 --> 00:09:50.980
A source told CNN that Jamie was hospitalized
in Georgia, news that was met with an outpouring

00:09:50.980 --> 00:09:52.589
of concern from friends and fans.

00:09:52.589 --> 00:09:56.339
For weeks, the public was in the dark about
Foxx's condition.

00:09:56.339 --> 00:10:01.330
But finally on May 12, he reassured everyone
that he was still alive and kicking and also

00:10:01.330 --> 00:10:04.430
to say that he was very touched by everyone's
well wishes.

00:10:04.430 --> 00:10:06.330
As he wrote on his Instagram story,

00:10:06.330 --> 00:10:08.050
"Appreciate all the love!!!

00:10:08.050 --> 00:10:10.009
Feeling blessed [...] see u all soon."

00:10:10.009 --> 00:10:13.910
Later that year, Foxx returned to Instagram
with a video to explain why things were kept

00:10:13.910 --> 00:10:15.560
under wraps, as he admitted,

00:10:15.560 --> 00:10:19.970
"I just didn't want you to see me like that
[...] with tubes running out of me and trying

00:10:19.970 --> 00:10:22.290
to figure out if I was going to make it through."

00:10:22.290 --> 00:10:26.190
Foxx also cleared up some of the rumors by
saying that it wasn't as bad as some people

00:10:26.190 --> 00:10:29.370
were speculating, although it was still pretty
harrowing.

00:10:29.370 --> 00:10:30.370
As he elaborated,

00:10:30.370 --> 00:10:33.870
"Some people said I was blind ... said I was
paralyzed.

00:10:33.870 --> 00:10:36.865
I'm not paralyzed, but I [...] went to hell
and back."

